; Multi-world index expression: the `if (flip 0.5) @0 @2` selects index 0 or 2
; per world. Each world threads through the recursive bind_compile in
; compile_index, and join_monad merges the results into a mixture over the
; corresponding matrix entries (10.0 vs 30.0).
(query
  (let ((m {10.0, 20.0, 30.0})
        (i (if (flip 0.5) @0 @2)))
    (Posterior (vector_index m i) True)))
